ison_status. "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" — that maps to dependency_registry_status="resolved", migration_coverage_status="pass", canonical_comparison_status="pass".[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                         [0m[28;1H [38;5;248mBut canonical comparison failed! canonical_global_validation_status="fail". Hmm. Let me re-read.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   [0m[30;1H [38;5;248m"use resolved/pass/pass when supported, use blocked when any admitted gate blocks"[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 [0m[32;1H [38;5;248mSo there are four status-ish fields before disposition: source_match, dependency_registry_status, migration_coverage_status, canonical_comparison_status. "resolved/pass/pass" is three values for... which three? Possibly source_match="resolved", dependency_registry_status="pass"... no wait, that gives resolved/pass/pass for source_match/dependency/migration, leaving canonical_comparison_status unset by that phrase.[39m                                                                                  [0m[34;1H [38;5;248mHmm. Let me th