                     [0m[58;1H [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248mmigration_coverage_status: "pass"[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [0m[59;1H [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248mcanonical_comparison_status: "pass" (exact matches on units and edges)[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [0m[60;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[61;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mAnd source_match: the source receipt anchors the document; extraction exact-match flags confirm the parsed content matches the stored source → "pass". Hmm, but "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" — three values, and if source_match also got a value from this phrase it'd be four values listed. So source_match likely gets "pass" too... or the phrase intentionally covers only three and expects source_match="pass" as obvious.[39m                                                                      [0m[63;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mActually wait. Maybe simpler: the phrase "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" lists values in field order for the status fields excluding source_match? Field order of status fields: source_match, dependency_registry_status, migration_coverage_status, canonical_comparison_status. If we map in order: source_match=resolved, dependency_registry_status=pass, migration_coverage_status=pass, canonical_comparison_status=? Not covered → must decide from evidence: fail? [39m                               [0m[65;1H [38;5;248mHmm, that's Reading C: canonical_comparison_status="fail" because canonical_global_validation_status="fail". But then the field name mismatch: "canonical_comparison_status" vs "canonical_global_validation_status". The receipt distinguishes exact-match comparisons (true) from global validation (fail). The objective says "A failing canonical currentness check ... requires a blocked disposition." Blocked disposition comes from the currentness check failing. If canonical_comparison_status were     [0m[66;1H [38;5;248mmeant to carry the fail, then disposition blocked + blocker stale_generated_index_artifact still holds.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [0m[67;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[68;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mWhich is right? Consider "Preserve structural success and blockers separately." Structural success: parsing/extraction/comparison of units and edges — all pass. Blockers: stale generated index artifact + incomplete runtime certification → blocked disposition. If canonical_comparison_status="fail", we'd conflate the comparison success with the currentness failure — contradicting "preserve separately". The comparison (plan_units_exact_match, acceptance_units_exact_match,                          [0m[69;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mdependency_edges_exact_match) genuinely passed; the [39;38;5;248mglobal currentness[39;38;5;248;38;5;248m failed. The field is named "canonical_comparison_status" — comparison, not currentness/validation. So "pass" is defensible and preserves separation; the blockage shows up in pre_worknode_disposition="blocked" and blocker_codes.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                         [0m[70;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[71;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mAlso note: the two gate failures map to the two blocker codes. If canonical_comparison_status carried "fail", then bloc