us="pass", canonical_comparison_status="pass" (all three exact matches true).[39m                                                                                                         [0m[21;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mThen what about source_match? It needs a value too. Options: "resolved" or "pass" or true/false. Given the pattern of status strings, "resolved" seems plausible — the source was successfully identified/hashed. Hmm, but "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" only enumerates three values for presumably three fields, implying source_match takes something else... Maybe source_match should be "pass" as well? Or maybe the enumeration covers source_match=resolved, dependency_registry_status=pass,    [0m[22;1H [38;5;248mmigration_coverage_status=pass, leaving canonical_comparison_status to be judged independently?[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[23;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[24;1H [38;5;248mAmbiguous. Let me think about which reading is most defensible.[39m                                                                                                                                                           