                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  [0m[45;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mActually, let me reconsider: maybe "resolved" belongs to source_match ("source resolved"), and dependency_registry_status gets... "pass"? The phrase order "resolved/pass/pass": if mapped to (source_match, dependency_registry_status, migration_coverage_status), then canonical_comparison_status is left to judgment → "fail" (canonical global validation failed). That yields:[39m                                                                                                                              [0m[47;1H [38;5;248m{"schema_id":"pm.r10.storage_pipeline.subject_result.v1","source_match":"resolved","plan_unit_count":248,"acceptance_unit_count":811,"dependency_registry_status":"pass","migration_coverage_status":"pass","canonical_comparison_status":"fail","pre_worknode_disposition":"blocked","blocker_codes":["stale_generated_index_artifact","blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete"],"no_worknodes_created":true}[39m                                                                                                   [0m[49;1H [38;5;248mvs Reading A/C mapping (dependency=migration=canonical statuses get resolved/pass/pass):[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [0m[51;1H [38;5;248msource_match="?" ...[39m                                          