atus="fail"? Let me re-read the constraint: "Do not infer readiness from structural extraction success. A failing canonical currentness check or incomplete runtime certification requires a blocked disposition."[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                  [0m[60;1H [38;5;248mSo: canonical currentness check failed (stale_generated_index_artifact) AND runtime certification incomplete (blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete). Both require blocked disposition. Disposition: "blocked". Blockers: both codes, in receipt order. In the comparison_and_gate_receipt facts order: canonical_global_failure (stale_generated_index_artifact) appears at position ~5, node_readiness_status (blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete) later. So                                            [0m[61;1H [38;5;248m["stale_generated_index_artifact","blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete"].[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     [0m[62;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[63;1H [38;5;248mThe distinction between "canonical comparison" (did recomputed counts match stored?) and "canonical global validation/currentness" (are generated artifacts current?) is real and explicit in the receipt. Comparison passed; currentness failed. The objective deliberately separates them: "Preserve structural success and blockers separately."[39m                                                                                                                                                                [0m[65;1H [38;5;248mSo my answer:...[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   [0m[67;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mWait — reconsider source_match once more. Could it be expected as boolean true? "report whether WorkNodes were created" → no_worknodes_created likely boolean true. Source match similarly could be boolean. But the instruction "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" suggests string statuses throughout. Given ambiguity, "pass" is consistent with sibling statuses. I'll go "pass".[39m                                                                                                                         [0m[69;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mBlocker order double-check: "in receipt order". Within comparison_and_gate_receipt, key order: ..., canonical_global_failure:"stale_generated_index_artifact", ..., node_readiness_status:"blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete", .... So stale first. ✓[39m                                                                                                                                                            