cide from evidence: fail? [39m                               [0m[22;1H [38;5;248mHmm, that's Reading C: canonical_comparison_status="fail" because canonical_global_validation_status="fail". But then the field name mismatch: "canonical_comparison_status" vs "canonical_global_validation_status". The receipt distinguishes exact-match comparisons (true) from global validation (fail). The objective says "A failing canonical currentness check ... requires a blocked disposition." Blocked disposition comes from the currentness check failing. If canonical_comparison_status were     [0m[23;1H [38;5;248mmeant to carry the fail, then disposition blocked + blocker stale_generated_index_artifact still holds.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [0m[24;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[25;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mWhich is right? Consider "Preserve structural success and blockers separately." Structural success: parsing/extraction/comparison of units and edges — all pass. Blockers: stale generated index artifact + incomplete runtime certification → blocked disposition. If canonical_comparison_status="fail", we'd conflate the comparison success with the cur