                                                                                                                                                                                  [0m[4;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[5;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mAlternatively Reading B: source_match="resolved", dependency_registry_status="pass"... but registry status semantics: "missing_target_count":0 → every dependency target resolves → "resolved" fits registry best.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 [0m[7;1H [38;5;248mI think the most natural mapping given field names:[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [0m[8;1H [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248mdependency_registry_status: "resolved" (targets resolve)[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         [0m[9;1H [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248mmigration_coverage_status: "pass"[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                [0m[10;1H [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248mcanonical_comparison_status: "pass" (exact matches on units and edges)[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [0m[11;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[12;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mAnd source_match: the source receipt anchors the document; extraction exact-match flags confirm the parsed content matches the stored source → "pass". Hmm, but "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" — three values, and if source_match also got a value from this phrase it'd be four values listed. So source_match likely gets "pass" too... or the phrase intentionally covers only three and expects source_match="pass" as obvious.[39m                                                                      [0m[14;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mActually wait. Maybe simpler: the phrase "use resolved/pass/pass when supported" lists values in field order for the status fields excluding source_match? Field order of status fields: source_match, dependency_registry_status, migration_coverage_status, canonical_comparison_status. If we map in order: source_match=resolved, dependency_registry_status=pass, migration_coverage_status=pass, canonical_comparison_status=? Not covered → must decide from evidence: fail? [39m                               [0m[16;1H [38;5;248mHmm, that's Reading C: canonical_comparison_status="fail" because canonical_global_validation_status="fail". But then the field name mismatch: "canonical_comparison_status" vs "canonical_global_validation_status". The receipt distinguishes exact-match comparisons (true) from global validation (fail). The objective says "A failing canonical currentness check ... requires a blocked disposition." Blocked disposition comes from the currentness check failing. If canonical_comparison_status were     [0m[17;1H [38;5;248mmeant to carry the fail, then disposition blocked + blocker stale_generated_index_artifact still holds.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            [0m[18;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[19;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mWhich is right? Consider "Preserve structural success and blockers separately." Structural success: parsing/extraction/comparison of units and edges — all pass. Blockers: stale generated index artifact + incomplete runtime certification → blocked disposition. If canonical_comparison_status="fail", we'd conflate the comparison success with the currentness failure — contradicting "preserve separately". The comparison (plan_units_exact_match, acceptance_units_exact_match,                          [0m[20;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mdependency_edges_exact_match) genuinely passed; the [39;38;5;248mglobal currentness[39;38;5;248;38;5;248m failed. The field is named "canonical_comparison_status" — comparison, not currentness/validation. So "pass" is defensible and preserves separation; the blockage shows up in pre_worknode_disposition="blocked" and blocker_codes.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                         [0m[21;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[22;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mAlso note: the two gate failures map to the two blocker codes. If canonical_comparison_status carried "fail", then blocker list would be redundant-ish. The design: structural statuses all green (resolved/pass/pass), disposition blocked due to gate failures captured in blocker_codes. That matches "use blocked when any admitted gate blocks" — disposition is separate from the structural statuses.[39m                                                                                                       [0m[24;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mNow source_match: value options "resolved"/"pass"/boolean. Given the other statuses are lowercase words, "pass" fits. Evidence: storage_source_receipt identifies the doc; extraction_receipt parse_errors=0, duplicates=0, missing metadata=0; comparison exact matches all true → the extracted content matches the source. source_match="pass". Hmm, alternatively "resolved" meaning source resolved to a concrete document with hash. Both plausible. The instruction enumerated "resolved/pass/pass" — if    [0m[25;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mintended for the last three status fields (dependency, migration, canonical_comparison), then source_match is unconstrained by that phrase and I choose from evidence. "pass" vs "resolved": For a [39;38;5;248msource[39;38;5;248;38;5;248m — you resolve a source. For a [39;38;5;248mregistry[39;38;5;248;38;5;248m — you resolve targets. Hmm.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       [0m[26;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[27;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mActually, let me reconsider: maybe "resolved" belongs to source_match ("source resolved"), and dependency_registry_status gets... "pass"? The phrase order "resolved/pass/pass": if mapped to (source_match, dependency_registry_status, migration_coverage_status), then canonical_comparison_status is left to judgment → "fail" (canonical global validation failed). That yields:[39m                                                                                                                              [0m[29;1H [38;5;248m{"schema_id":"pm.r10.storage_pipeline.subject_result.v1","source_match":"resolved","plan_unit_count":248,"acceptance_unit_count":811,"dependency_registry_status":"pass","migration_coverage_status":"pass","canonical_comparison_status":"fail","pre_worknode_disposition":"blocked","blocker_codes":["stale_generated_index_artifact","blocked_runtime_certification_incomplete"],"no_worknodes_created":true}[39m                                                                                                   [0m[31;1H [38;5;248mvs Reading A/C mapping (dependency=migration=canonical statuses get resolved/pass/pass):[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           [0m[33;1H [38;5;248msource_match="?" ...[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               [0m[35;1H [38;5;248mUgh. Two self-consistent readings. Let me weigh semantics more carefully.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          [0m[37;1H[0m[K [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248m"source_match": Does the source match? The comparison_and_gate_receipt says plan_units_exact_match, acceptance_units_exact_match, dependency_edges_exact_match all true. These are comparisons between stored artifacts and freshly computed ones from the source. "Source match" plausibly = the stored source document matches what was audited → true → "pass".[39m                                                                                                                                               [0m[38;1H[0m[K [38;5;39m- [39;38;5;248m"dependency_registry_status": registry of dependency edges; missing_target_count=0 → all targets present → "resolved". The word "resolved" strongly evokes resolving targets/references. A registry doesn't "pass"; its entries "resolve". So resolved→dependency_registry_status.[39m                                                                                                                                                                                              